## Build base

**llama.cpp / ggml**
- Source: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
- Licence: MIT — Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors

**llama-cpp-turboquant (TurboQuant + MTP integration)**
- Source: https://github.com/TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant
- Pinned: tag `tqp-v0.4.0`, commit `bcb85fc3ae85efa0f5f392c6c880dfc524923860`
- Licence: MIT — Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors
- Notes: this fork carries the C/CUDA implementation of TurboQuant (WHT rotation
  plus PolarQuant scalar quantisation, `ggml/src/ggml-turbo-quant.c`,
  `ggml/src/ggml-cuda/turbo*.{cu,cuh}`) and the upstream MTP speculative
  decoding path. TurboQuant as a method originates from Google Research,
  *Online Vector Quantization with Near-optimal Distortion Rate* (ICLR 2026).
  This project claims no authorship over either.

**Local patch** `config/buildCMD/patches/0001-json-object-grammar.patch`
- Modifies `tools/server/server-common.cpp` of the above (MIT), and is therefore
  distributed under the same MIT terms.
- What it fixes: a request with `response_format={"type":"json_object"}` and no
  `schema` field resolves to `{}`, which the JSON-grammar path treats as "no
  response format at all", so no grammar is generated and clients get prose back.

